/**
 * GET /api/v1/public/receipts/[receiptId] — Public Receipt Proof
 *
 * Unauthenticated endpoint that returns the proof-only fields of a receipt.
 * This is the backend for shareable receipt URLs (permissionprotocol.com/r/:id).
 *
 * SECURITY INVARIANTS:
 * 1. NO authentication required (receipts are public proof)
 * 2. Returns ONLY proof fields — never secrets, parameters, or internal IDs
 * 3. Rate-limited per IP to prevent scraping
 * 4. Immutable data — cacheable with long TTL
 *
 * DESIGN RATIONALE:
 * Receipts are the core primitive of Permission Protocol. They must be
 * independently verifiable by anyone, anywhere, without authenticating
 * with PP. This is the same pattern as certificate transparency logs
 * or Stripe publishable receipt URLs. The proof is public; the issuance
 * is private.
